type: software
title: "A sharp stop-loss bound for Rademacher sums, the constant two in a concave comparison, and local extremal sets on the discrete cube"
abstract: "Unrefereed research candidate. For a Rademacher sum S of unit variance, E(|S| - t)+ <= (sqrt(2) - t)/2 for every t in [1/sqrt(2), 201/200], with equality only for two equal weights and a quadratic stability estimate. This proves Lowther's proposed bound, so Kontorovich's concave comparison holds with the sharp constant 2 (also in Hilbert space), and improves Kontorovich's total-variation tensorization constant from 0.1798 to 0.1967. On the discrete cube it gives the local structure of sets of maximal first-level Fourier weight near densities 1/4 and 1/8, partly assuming an unrefereed 2026 theorem of Lei Yu."
